# Competency question (native gmeow:reasoningLogic lane): the coboundary dual of the
# boundary square-zero question. Firing math:coboundarySquareZeroLaw over the pre-reified
# coface atoms of the triangle DERIVES the binary consequent
# math:coCancellingPairRel(edgeAB, edgeAC) — the two intermediate cofaces of the upward
# co-diamond over (vertexA, faceABC) with opposite sign products. That triple exists in
# the reasoned closure ONLY because the law fired; nothing asserts it. VALUES pins the
# query to edgeAB so the answer is exactly one row {edgeAB, edgeAC}. Removing the law
# formula makes the answer empty.
PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX excc: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/chain-complex/>

SELECT ?b ?bp WHERE {
    VALUES ?b { excc:edgeAB }
    ?b math:coCancellingPairRel ?bp .
}
